    "title": "Four sign at Mater Dei on National Signing Day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ronald Clark ,\n30 minutes ago\nEVANSVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) – Mater Dei high school opened their gym to host four student athletes who signed their letter of intent to play at the next level on national signing day.\nWildcats’ star softball player, Baylee Maurer signed to play at Lincoln Land Community College in Springfield, Illinois.\nWhile her teammate, Macy Lankford is headed to Canton, Illinois to play at Spoon River College.\nMorgan Wannemuehler is staying in town signing with the University of Southern Indiana to play soccer.\n“It felt really special to me, because I’m glad they got to watch me and they’re going to be able to watch me for the next four years,” Wannemuehler said about her teammates. “Cause many of them are younger and I just feel like a really good role model for them.”\nShay Straus was the final student athlete of the group. She signed to play soccer at Division II Rockhurst University in Kansas City.\nStraus said, “Obviously there’s stress with you know all your friends are going to IU or Purdue and it’s like I’m going to lose all my friends. but just knowing I’m not alone, I’m not the only one that’s going to choose a different path. So it definitely felt a little more less stressful.”\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
